{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8226920",
      "title": "Preparing Another Use-Case For useEffect",
      "sourceHash": "7e3abc514c5672d7857db0eeaecfaea9b5dd70adb9548e807b4d34463578b89f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.57,
          "en": "So now that we got started with side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.57,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "that need and that don't need useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "let's take a closer look at useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.963,
          "en": "and especially at this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "And for that, let's switch to this modal component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 22.29,
          "en": "In there I got some code using the useImperativeHandle hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "that ensures that we expose two methods, two functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 31.79,
          "en": "to the outside world here, a open and a closed function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 35.07,
          "en": "And these functions will then internally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.07,
          "end": 40.07,
          "en": "in this modal component, show or close the dialog element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 44.133,
          "en": "which is also controlled with help of our ref here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 49.26,
          "en": "So these exposed functions, these methods here ,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 49.26,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "are used in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "There I have code where I call open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 57.453,
          "en": "and I have code where I call close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "And my goal now is to actually handle this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 66.06,
          "en": "with help of an effect, with help of a side effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 66.06,
          "end": 69.84,
          "en": "So with help of the useEffect hook, because as you'll see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.84,
          "end": 73.59,
          "en": "that's all the possible in situations like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "And therefore here I'll get rid of this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 79.863,
          "en": "useImperativeHandle code, I'll delete it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 83.883,
          "en": "And also delete this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.81,
          "end": 87.09,
          "en": "And also get rid of this ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 88.803,
          "en": "because I don't need it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.82,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "And what we could now do as an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "to the old approach is that this modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 101.55,
          "en": "accepts a prop, let's say a prop named open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.55,
          "end": 104.013,
          "en": "though the name, of course, is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.33,
          "end": 110.33,
          "en": "Now as it turns out, the dialog element also has a open prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "built into this element which we could then set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 117.93,
          "en": "to our open prop assuming that open is true or false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 117.93,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "because that is what the open prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 121.893,
          "en": "of the dialog element wants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.18,
          "en": "And with that change, we could go back to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.18,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "And now instead of opening and closing that modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 134.68,
          "en": "with help of the modal ref, we could delete this ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 139.07999999999998,
          "en": "and instead manage some extra state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 139.07999999999998,
          "end": 142.293,
          "en": "which controls whether the modal should be open or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "Initially it should be false so that the modal is not open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 152.177,
          "en": "And here we could say IsOpen and set IsOpen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "And maybe name it ModalIsOpen to be clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 159.963,
          "en": "what exactly is open or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 161.55,
          "end": 164.73,
          "en": "And now in all the places where I called open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 164.73,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "we should now call setModalIsOpen and set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 171.78,
          "en": "And in all the places where we called close,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 175.683,
          "en": "we should now call setModalIsOpen and set it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 178.36,
          "end": 180.933,
          "en": "Of course, also down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 185.82,
          "en": "Now we can use the modalIsOpen state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 185.82,
          "end": 189.064,
          "en": "and pass it as a value to this open prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.064,
          "end": 190.064,
          "en": "modalIsOpen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 191.7,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "And we should remove this ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 196.053,
          "en": "because we don't have this modal ref anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "If we save that, you'll see that if I now click on an item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 204.51,
          "en": "the modal does indeed open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 204.51,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "but the backdrop is actually missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "This area behind the modal that grays out the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "and makes sure that we can't interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "with the rest of the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 215.88,
          "end": 217.803,
          "en": "This backdrop is missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "And it's missing because this backdrop is only added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "by the dialog element if we open it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 229.623,
          "en": "by calling the dialog's showModal method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 234.963,
          "en": "Only when we call this method will this backdrop be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 236.07,
          "end": 239.76,
          "en": "So therefore forwarding this open prop to the dialog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 239.76,
          "end": 242.943,
          "en": "as we're currently doing it does not really work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 247.68,
          "en": "But we can still stick to this prop focused solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 249.903,
          "en": "by again using useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}